cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ladder in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ladder: empirical model routing for recurring LLM work"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Amit
    family-names: Kumar
    alias: growthperclick
    website: "https://iamamitkumar.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RavenRepo/ladder"
url: "https://ravenrepo.github.io/ladder/"
abstract: >-
  ladder runs recurring LLM work on the cheapest model tier that still passes
  an external, cross-family verifier gate. It trials cheaper rungs on a fraction
  of dispatches and promotes or demotes each capability from counted,
  externally verified outcomes instead of predicted difficulty.
keywords:
  - LLM cost optimization
  - model routing
  - LLM evaluation
  - cross-family verification
  - LLMOps
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
